<title>RUSSIA: Russian 322-day T-bill yields 30.64 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 322-day T-bill yields 30.64 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 322-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 30.64 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the yield would be in a 29.5-30.7 percent range.</p>
<p>The 23003 bills, maturing on March 4 next year, the closest maturity to the new issue, closed at 79.65 on Tuesday, to yield 30.18 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number		   22081</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		  8.20 trln</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)		     6.40 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)		  6.76 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds			  5.32 trln</p>
<p>    Average price		   78.72 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	 78.50 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		   30.64 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	31.05 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			     322 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   March 18, 1998</p>
<p>On April 30 the Finance Ministry will offer four trillion roubles of OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24012). It will also repay about 6.87 trillion roubles in maturing 224-day T-bills (series 23050).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
